li_poi Module
=============

Lawful interception: the target match of a point of interception (IRI-POI)
in an IMS signalling function, 3GPP TS 33.128 clause 7.12.

The module does not copy or send messages. It holds a table of digests of
target identifiers and tells the script whether a request belongs to an
intercepted communication. The script then copies the transaction with the
tracer module to the X2/X3 forwarder of the pod, which delivers it as
IMSMessage xIRI (ETSI TS 103 221-2):

    loadmodule "proto_hep.so"
    loadmodule "tracer.so"
    loadmodule "li_poi.so"
    modparam("li_poi", "socket", "/run/li/poi.sock")
    modparam("proto_hep", "hep_id", "[li_fwd] 127.0.0.1:9062;transport=udp;version=3")
    modparam("tracer", "trace_id", "[li_trace] uri=hep:li_fwd")

    route {
        if (li_match($var(li)))
            trace("li_trace", "t", "sip", , , $var(li));
        ...
    }

Who is intercepted must not be visible to those who operate the platform.
The module therefore has no MI commands, no statistics and no log line that
depends on a target, and the table holds digests, never identifiers.

Parameters
----------

socket (string, required)
    Unix socket of the X2/X3 forwarder. The module connects to it from a
    process of its own and receives the task table: after the connection is
    made and after every change (format in li_table.h). While the forwarder
    is away the last table stays in use.

call_ttl (integer, default 7200)
    Seconds an INVITE that matched stays known by its Call-ID. Every later
    request of the call renews it.

Functions
---------

li_match(result)
    Request route. Returns 1 if the request belongs to an intercepted
    communication, -1 otherwise. With an empty table and no remembered call
    it returns at once, without parsing anything.

    Match (TS 33.128 clause 7.12.2.8.2), for targets given as IMPU:
      - From and P-Asserted-Identity: the target is the sender
      - Request-URI and To: the target is the receiver
      - the Call-ID of an INVITE that matched before

    An identity is compared in a canonical form (li_identity.h): a tel URI
    and a SIP URI with the same E.164 number are the same identity.

    On a match, result is set to

        v1;d=<f|t|c|i>;m=<f|t|u>;x=<xid>[,<xid>...]

    d  direction of the session: from the target, to the target, combined,
       indeterminate (a request in a dialog whose INVITE this instance did
       not see)
    m  direction of this request: from the target, to the target, unknown.
       A request outside a dialog that is known only by its Call-ID has the
       direction of its session.
    x  the tasks (XIDs), 32 hex digits each, at most 8

    The value is meant as the correlation_id of trace(); the forwarder reads
    it from the HEP correlation chunk.

Limits
------

- Targets given as IMPI or IMEI are not matched yet.
- The Call-ID memory is per instance: in a cluster, a request in a dialog
  that reaches another instance is matched by its headers only.

Tests
-----

    cc -Wall -Wextra -o /tmp/identity_test test/identity_test.c li_identity.c && /tmp/identity_test
    cc -Wall -Wextra -o /tmp/table_test test/table_test.c li_table.c && /tmp/table_test

The vectors of identity_test.c are shared with the X1 agent of the platform
(li_x1_identity.erl). End-to-end tests with OpenSIPS are in the helm
repository: apps/li-x2x3-forwarder/integration/test_opensips.py.
